        "headline": "Winter Weather Advisory issued May 30 at 6:35AM AKDT until May 30 at 9:00AM AKDT by NWS Anchorage AK",
        "description": "* WHAT...Snow. Snow accumulations up to two inches. Visibility as\nlow as one quarter mile in heavy wet snow.\n\n* WHERE...Eureka / Tahneta Pass.\n\n* WHEN...Until 9 AM AKDT this morning.\n\n* IMPACTS...Travel could be very difficult.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...A band of heavy wet snow has developed over\nthe Glenn Highway from mile marker 115 to mile marker 130 - from\nSheep Mountain to Eureka. Snow is expected to continue over the\narea through mid morning before tapering off. Up to two inches of\nsnow has ",
